  "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $a.$ To do this, we first add $2$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =-14ab-2 \\\\ 5+2 & =-14ab-2+2 \\\\ 7 & =-14ab\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-14b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =-14ab \\\\ \\frac{7}{-14b} & =\\frac{-14ab}{-14b} \\\\ \\frac{7}{-14b} & =\\frac{\\cancel{-14b}a}{\\cancel{-14b}} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{14b} & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the right-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7}{7\\cdot 2b} & =a \\\\ -\\frac{\\cancel{7}}{\\cancel{7}\\cdot 2b} & =a \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2b} & =a \\\\ a & =-\\frac{1}{2b}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
